# "World" occurs at 1-based index 8 and again at 15. Ropes.Index's
# Backward direction requires a match to fit entirely within Source
# (First .. From) -- one stricter than RopeTool.Mod's own rfind bound
# by Pattern'Length - 1 (see PLAN.md's "Search" section) -- so FROM=13
# is chosen directly against that formula (verified against a real
# run, not derived by just shifting RopeTool.Mod's own FROM=13 by one)
# rather than assumed to carry over unchanged; it happens to still
# exclude the second match and find the first, same as the original.
program rope_tool
arg rindex
arg Hello, World! World!
arg World
arg 13
status 0
output
8
